## Migrations

Alembic reads its database URL from `Settings` (`src/{{ package_name }}/core/config.py`),
the same object the app itself reads — never point a migration at a different
database than the app runs against, and never hardcode a connection string in
`alembic.ini` or a migration file.

```bash
make revision m="add users"   # autogenerate, then read the diff before trusting it
make migrate                  # apply to head
```
{% endif %}

## Conventions

- Ruff and `mypy --strict` are both enforced in CI (`make check`); run it
  before committing rather than finding out there.
- Settings come from the environment via pydantic-settings
  (`{{ env_prefix }}*` variables) — don't read `os.environ` directly in
  application code, and don't hardcode anything secret as a default.
- Tests run against SQLite in memory (`tests/conftest.py`), so `make test`
  needs nothing else running. A new endpoint or model needs a test that
  exercises it through those fixtures, not a new ad hoc setup.
- `/health/live` and `/health/ready` are separate on purpose — don't collapse
  them, an orchestrator needs to tell "restart me" from "don't route to me
  yet" apart.
{% if has_addon('pre-commit') %}
## Before committing

`pre-commit install` once per clone. If a hook fails, fix what it flagged
rather than skipping it with `--no-verify`.
